      This very pleasant 79-year-old female significant past medical history of CVA in adulthood, as well as multiple TIAs, CKD, DM 2, HTN, macular degeneration presents to the emergency department with concerns of blurred vision and weakness.  Patient usually walks with a cane and kind of drags her right leg however today patient was unable to ambulate.  Patient also having some increased blurred vision although she has fairly blurred vision already but it was just slightly worse.  Patient was brought to the ER for further evaluation.  When I saw patient at bedside she was alert and oriented x 4 and I noticed no focal neurological deficits that were new on exam.  Patient was watching NCIS as she is watched every season at least 4 times.  We did have lengthy discussions about this because I watch NCIS as well.  Patient actually quite pleasurable to talk to.



